# Integrated Agile Workflow

## Core Components

### 1. Agile Workflow Structure
- Epics → Stories → Tasks → Subtasks
- Management in `.ai/` directory
- Approval-based progress management

### 2. Rule System
- Automation rules in `.cursor/rules/`
- Priority-based execution
- Evolution through version control

### 3. LDD (Logging-Driven Development)
- Log management in `.logs/`
- Structured log templates
- Integrated feedback loop

### 4. Memory Bank
- Tracking project state
- Accumulation of learnings
- Management of optimization history

## Integrated Workflow

### Phase 1: Initialization
1. Environment verification
   - Existence of `.ai/` directory
   - Placement of required templates
   - Rule file validation

2. Context setting
   - Recording project information
   - Setting initial metrics
   - Establishing log structure

### Phase 2: Planning
1. PRD creation/update
   - Requirement definition
   - Epic identification
   - Priority setting

2. Architecture design
   - Technology selection
   - Structural design
   - Constraint definition

### Phase 3: Execution
1. Story management
   - Task breakdown
   - Progress tracking
   - Feedback collection

2. Implementation process
   - Test-driven development
   - Continuous validation
   - Documentation updates

### Phase 4: Optimization
1. Metrics analysis
   - Performance evaluation
   - Quality indicator tracking
   - Efficiency measurement

2. Rule adjustment
   - Feedback reflection
   - Auto-tuning
   - Version updates

## Integration Rules

<rules>
1. All tasks must have appropriate log entries
2. Feedback is immediately reflected in the memory bank
3. Rule updates are automatically propagated
4. Metrics are continuously collected and analyzed
5. Optimization is performed regularly
</rules>

## Metrics Definition

### 1. Project Metrics
- Epic completion rate
- Story progress status
- Task completion velocity

### 2. Quality Metrics
- Test coverage
- Code quality score
- Documentation completeness

### 3. Process Metrics
- Feedback loop efficiency
- Rule optimization effectiveness
- Learning rate indicator

## Feedback Loop

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Task Execution] --> B[Log Recording]
    B --> C[Metrics Collection]
    C --> D[Analysis & Evaluation]
    D --> E[Rule Optimization]
    E --> F[Memory Update]
    F --> A
```

## Optimization Mechanism

### 1. Rule Optimization
- Usage frequency analysis
- Effectiveness measurement
- Automatic adjustment

### 2. Process Optimization
- Bottleneck identification
- Efficiency proposals
- Automation enhancement

### 3. Context Optimization
- Memory usage efficiency
- Learning efficiency
- Feedback efficiency

<critical>
- All components must always maintain synchronization
- Optimization is performed automatically and continuously
- Feedback is reflected immediately
- Metrics are always kept up-to-date
</critical>